  "protocol": "Three fresh installations per workload and firmware, split 2+1 across two boots of each variant. Four OTA boots in standard, pairs, standard, pairs order. One module at a time, telemetry export off. The standard variant uses the stock 32-bit fast-interpreter dispatch with the common firmware integration patches. The pairs variant preserves the 32-bit records and inserts direct jumps for 35 adjacent opcode combinations, using the regular scalar handlers and instruction metering. Richards and DeltaBlue return the median of three batches of ten iterations, divided by ten here. For DeltaBlue only the execute phase contributes to the score. CoreMark is the 64 KiB wasm3 catalog module.",
